The dungeon has several branches.  The gnomish mines you were
in is the earliest one.  The next one starts with an extra up
stairs and there are several other branches throughout the game.
Each branch has something of importance that you'll eventually
need to puzzle out.

> I found delphi which was really weird as it had ghosts from two
> previous characters.

When you die there's a chance of leaving a bones file.  When you
enter a new level there's a chance of loading a stored bones file
for that level.  On a multi-user system they could even come
from other players.  One point of this is the game tends to keep
handing you the same problem again and again until you puzzle
out how to solve it, but since everything is random it's possible
to keep playing again and again until that bones file goes away.
Trying forever again is a valid approach to problem solving, but
learning each time works even better.

